**🩺 Stability & Availability** | **🟠 Major** | **⚡ Quick win**

**Revoked `.repairing` jobs stay unfinished forever.**

`revoke(_:)` handles only `.queued` jobs that are not active, plus `.awaitingActivation` and `.awaitingClarification` jobs. For a `.repairing` job, the code sets `revoked = true` and leaves the stage unchanged. `kick()` then removes revoked records from scheduling (`records.values.filter { !$0.revoked }`). As a result, the job never runs again and never reaches a terminal stage.

A job reaches `.repairing` in three ways:
- the TV sends an activation diagnostic (`requestActivated` with `diagnostic`);
- `suspend()` runs during sleep or quit;
- `load()` recovers an interrupted job.

If an operator revokes the TV while the job is in that state, the job stays non-terminal. `verify`, `disable`, `chooseFolder`, `reload`, and `load` all refuse to run while any job is non-terminal. `cancelQueued` accepts only `.queued`. The Mac then stays locked until someone edits `journal.json` by hand.

Make every non-active, non-terminal revoked job terminal. Apply the same rule when a suspended active job is later revoked.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
--- "a/HolodeckCore/Sources/HolodeckCore/ShaderRequestService.swift"
+++ "b/HolodeckCore/Sources/HolodeckCore/ShaderRequestService.swift"
@@ -258,17 +258,18 @@
         guard records[id]?.status.stage.terminal == true else { throw ShaderRequestError.invalidRequest }
         try FileManager.default.removeItem(at: folder(id)); records[id] = nil; try persist()
     }
     public func revoke(_ deviceID: String) throws {
         for id in records.keys where records[id]?.status.deviceID == deviceID && records[id]?.status.stage.terminal == false {
             records[id]?.revoked = true
-            if records[id]?.status.stage == .queued, activeID != id {
+            guard activeID != id else { continue }
+            if records[id]?.status.stage == .queued {
                 try update(id, stage: .cancelled, message: "TV access was revoked")
-            } else if records[id]?.status.stage == .awaitingActivation || records[id]?.status.stage == .awaitingClarification {
+            } else {
                 try update(id, stage: .failed, message: "TV access was revoked; any pushed commit remains")
             }
         }
         try persist()
     }

     public func control(operation: String, payload: ShaderRequestControl, deviceID: String) async throws -> ShaderRequestControlReply {
         try load()
```

`execute` must also mark a revoked job as `.failed` when it exits with `suspended == true`. Otherwise `suspend()` leaves that job in `.repairing`.
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

